%N A140389 Composite numbers k = 6*x - 5 such that x and 6*x - 1 are also composite.
%C A140389 x=c(i)=i-th composite and y=c(j)=j-th composite.
%e A140389 If x=16 and y=95, then (3*16*95-95-6)/(3*16+1)=4459/49=91=a(1).
%e A140389 If x=20 and y=119, then (3*20*119-119-6)/(3*20+1)=7015/61=115=a(2).
%e A140389 If x=21 and y=125, then (3*21*125-125-6)/(3*21+1)=7744/64=121=a(3).
%e A140389 If x=35 and y=209, then (3*35*209-209-6)/(3*35+1)=21730/106=205=a(4).
%e A140389 If x=50 and y=299, then (3*50*299-299-6)/(3*50+1)=44545/151=295=a(5).
%e A140389 If x=51 and y=305, then (3*51*305-305-6)/(3*51+1)=46354/154=301=a(6),
%e A140389 etc.
